      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a modern democracy, I suggest focusing on **epistemic humility**—the willingness to admit when you don't know something and adjust your beliefs. Alongside this, **intellectual empathy**, the capacity to genuinely consider differing perspectives even if you disagree with them, is crucial. Finally, **civic responsibility**, which involves actively participating and upholding shared norms, balances the abstract virtues. These traits help prevent polarization and foster reasoned public discourse.",
